nodecode-myradio is a rewrite of newjordan's newjordan/myradio:

  https://github.com/newjordan/myradio
  commit 66d611bad24f069a41b136b0672b39b9ab3cde12
  Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 Omnispace Technologies and the myradio contributors (LICENSE)

The original is a Hermes Agent plugin at integrations/hermes: a Python plugin
that starts myradio's own MCP adapter as a child process, sends one MCP
exchange over its stdin and reads the answer, and registers twelve tools, a
pre_tool_call hook, the /radio command, a myradio CLI command, a DJ skill and
a DJ-shift automation blueprint.

This rewrite keeps what a user of it got: the same twelve tools with the same
names, descriptions and arguments; the station status trimmed the same way for
a model; the library search; the same /radio words; and the rule that going
live, going off air and deleting audio stay the owner's. It is written in
Common Lisp and talks to the station over the same HTTP API the studio and that
adapter use -- loopback, the control.token from the station's data folder as
the token header -- so no Python, no adapter and no subprocess are needed. The
boxed 58-column ansi card is a plain aligned card here, and the DJ guidance
that was a skill is (help :myradio).

Left out, and why: the pre_tool_call hook that limited what an unattended
scheduled run could do -- Nodecode's own cron cell has no run context a cell
can read, so the hook would have nothing to gate on; the `myradio` CLI
command, which only reprinted the card; the automation blueprint, which is a
scheduling feature of the other harness; and the optional model-written song
lyrics on /radio request, which fall back to the original's own
plain-request path (the model can write the words and call myradio_make).
